{**
 * c-badge - a short label attached to something else: a state, a count, a name.
 *
 * It says what a thing is, never how loud it should be. "accent" is the variant
 * for a badge that carries the page's own subject; "danger" is for a state that
 * asks for attention - an invoice past its date, a product that ran out, an
 * account that was suspended - and is the word c-notice uses for a refusal. A
 * theme decides what either looks like.
 *
 * A variant nobody drew is refused rather than drawn as a plain badge: a state
 * that asks for attention and quietly looks like every other one is the kind of
 * mistake nobody notices.
 *}

{define badge, string $label, string $variant = 'plain', ?string $testId = null}
    {do Trilobit\Core\Presentation\Component\Argument::oneOf('c-badge', 'variant', $variant, ['plain', 'accent', 'danger'])}

    <span n:class="'c-badge', $variant !== 'plain' ? 'c-badge--' . $variant" data-testid="{$testId}">{$label}</span>
{/define}
